BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Lockwood-Mathews Mansion Museum to open its 2026 Season with a
  new exhibition on Irish American Art with a loan courtesy of Quinnipiac U
 niversity in conjunction with IGHMF
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260312
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260907
DTSTAMP:20260820T112406Z
UID:da14d852c63a67abe1d2079c1036@ctvisit-calendar
DESCRIPTION:With a loan courtesy of Quinnipiac University\, in conjunction
  with Ireland’s Great Hunger Museum of Fairfield\, the Lockwood-Mathews 
 Mansion Museum is currently showing a new exhibition titled\, “A Journey
  of Hope: The Irish American Immigrant Experience.” The exhibit will run
  through Sept. 6\, 2026\, and feature paintings and sculptures displayed i
 n the Mansion’s Art Gallery as well as in the Servants’ Quarters. View
 ing will be included with the purchase of a guided tour.\n\nSource: https:
 //ctvisit.com/events/lockwood-mathews-mansion-museum-open-its-2026-season-
 new-exhibition-irish-american-art-loan
LOCATION:Lockwood Mathews Mansion Museum\, 295 West Avenue\, Norwalk CT\, 
 06850
URL:https://ctvisit.com/events/lockwood-mathews-mansion-museum-open-its-20
 26-season-new-exhibition-irish-american-art-loan
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Norwich Stories of the American Revolution
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260509
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270101
DTSTAMP:20260820T112406Z
UID:c5d13aef0c36e1820a30a1a8eed9@ctvisit-calendar
DESCRIPTION:Norwich\, Connecticut was a center of Revolutionary activity i
 n Eastern Connecticut. From bands of Sons of Liberty to dedicated soldiers
  of all backgrounds\, the city produced scores of men and women who served
  in all capacities. From humble militiamen to a Signer of the Declaration 
 of Independence\, come and learn the lesser-known stories of these valiant
  Patriots as well as the story of America’s most infamous traitor\, Bene
 dict Arnold.\n\nSource: https://ctvisit.com/events/norwich-stories-america
 n-revolution
LOCATION:Slater Memorial Museum\, 108 Crescent Street\, Norwich CT\, 06360
URL:https://ctvisit.com/events/norwich-stories-american-revolution
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Sharks Exhibition
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260509
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270101
DTSTAMP:20260820T112406Z
UID:e900bdd06c9878548021b8ca7c6d@ctvisit-calendar
DESCRIPTION:People have been fascinated by sharks for as long as we have e
 xplored the ocean\, and now the Connecticut Science Center is bringing tha
 t fascination to life in the limited-time exhibition\, Sharks. This immers
 ive experience brings you face-to-face with some of the ocean’s most fas
 cinating predators through full-scale shark models\, interactive experienc
 es\, underwater environments\, ancient fossils\, immersive media\, and —
  of course — a lot of teeth.\n\nSource: https://ctvisit.com/events/shark
 s-exhibition
LOCATION:Connecticut Science Center\, 250 Columbus Boulevard\, Hartford CT
 \, 06103
URL:https://ctvisit.com/events/sharks-exhibition
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
